From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:14:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] sync: expose websocket transport timing metrics

Correlate WebSocket pings and pongs with bounded, connection-local diagnostic
IDs so delayed or out-of-order replies cannot inherit a newer ping's start
time. Ping payloads are diagnostic correlation IDs only. Unmatched pongs
still count for liveness and pong totals, but do not produce RTT samples;
matching consumes an entry so duplicate replies cannot add samples.

Expose queue delay, serialization, and socket flush as distinct timing
boundaries. Include oversized transition serialization before chunk encoding,
and distinguish socket-send success, error, and cancellation. Queue delay
retains its existing per-message observation point, including preparation and
earlier sends for chunked transitions. Socket-send timing excludes browser
acknowledgement and does not prove client receipt or application processing.

Keep the change wire-compatible with older clients through ordinary
WebSocket ping payload echoing; application sync messages and liveness
timeouts are unchanged. No schema or data migration, Caddy change, worker
change, or configuration change is required.

Document independent adoption, metric interpretation, rollback, and focused
verification. Keep this transport patch separate from runtime observability
and the final optional Wasm execution patch.
